cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use puremacro in your research or teaching, please cite it as below."
title: "puremacro: Production-grade Macroeconometric and Heterogeneous-Agent Structural Modeling in Pure Python"
version: 1.7.0
date-released: 2026-08-23
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/jalonso1979/puremacro"
url: "https://jalonso1979.github.io/puremacro/"
authors:
  - family-names: "Alonso Ortiz"
    given-names: "Jorge"
    affiliation: "Instituto Tecnológico Autónomo de México (ITAM), Mexico City, Mexico"
keywords:
  - "macroeconomics"
  - "econometrics"
  - "vector autoregression"
  - "HANK"
  - "nowcasting"
  - "climate macroeconomics"
  - "DICE"
  - "pyodide"
  - "webassembly"
abstract: >-
  puremacro is a self-contained, zero-C-extension macroeconomic computing library
  built in pure Python and NumPy. It unifies structural models (Sequence-Space HANK,
  DMP search-and-matching, continuous-time HJB), high-dimensional econometrics
  (FAVAR, Minnesota BVAR, Narrative Signs), mixed-frequency nowcasting, penalized
  forecasting (Elastic Net, Adaptive Lasso), and climate-macro integration (DICE).
  It runs identically in local environments, cloud clusters, and client-side in
  the browser via Pyodide.
